    "description": "Bipartite graph with parts of sizes 10 and 10, 66 edges, whose bipartite adjacency matrix has no 3x4 all-ones submatrix (no 3 vertices on the row side share 4 common neighbours). Witness for the extremal value z(10,10;3,4) = 66 (Towell 2026, OEIS A006615). The condition is asymmetric: a K_{3,4} occurs in the transposed 4x3 orientation, which z(m,n;3,4) permits, so the graph is not K_{3,4}-free as an abstract graph.",
    "reference": "A. Towell, 'Three new Zarankiewicz numbers z(m,n;3,4)', Zenodo 10.5281/zenodo.19985042 (2026)."
